IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `or336-nouns`
IMPORT `or336-seat`

-- Cases for the employee's seat layer (or336-seat.l4): Art. 336, 336a, 336b OR.
--
-- One scenario per case. Every input of the question is stated, so that no
-- value is hidden in a default; where a fact does not matter to the question,
-- it is FALSE or a placeholder date, and the scenario's comment says what the
-- case is about. The expected value of every case was written from the German
-- text before the file was run, never copied from a run. A case whose
-- expected value is NOTHING shows where the text does not decide.
--
-- Cases appear in the order of the Articles. The mirror cases, the same facts
-- put to the employer's seat, are in or336-cases-seat-employer.l4, and
-- or336-cases-mirror.l4 asserts that the two seats give the same answer.

§ `Cases for the employee's seat`

-- Notice because of a characteristic of the person who received it, not connected with the employment and no impairment: abusive, Art 336(1)(a).
`As the employee, case 1 (1a)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of a personal characteristic (Art 336(1)(a))` WITH
        `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS TRUE
        `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS FALSE
        `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 1 (1a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The characteristic is connected with the employment: the exception of 'es sei denn' is met, so not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 2 (1a)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of a personal characteristic (Art 336(1)(a))` WITH
        `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS TRUE
        `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS TRUE
        `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 2 (1a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business: the other exception is met.
`As the employee, case 3 (1a)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of a personal characteristic (Art 336(1)(a))` WITH
        `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS TRUE
        `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS FALSE
        `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 3 (1a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The notice was not given because of a characteristic: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 4 (1a)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of a personal characteristic (Art 336(1)(a))` WITH
        `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS FALSE
        `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS FALSE
        `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 4 (1a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice because the other party exercised a constitutional right, no exception: abusive, Art 336(1)(b).
`As the employee, case 5 (1b)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because a constitutional right was exercised (Art 336(1)(b))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS TRUE
        `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS FALSE
        `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 5 (1b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The exercise of the right breached a duty from the employment: the exception is met.
`As the employee, case 6 (1b)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because a constitutional right was exercised (Art 336(1)(b))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS TRUE
        `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS TRUE
        `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 6 (1b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The exercise of the right substantially impaired cooperation in the business: the exception is met.
`As the employee, case 7 (1b)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because a constitutional right was exercised (Art 336(1)(b))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS TRUE
        `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS FALSE
        `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 7 (1b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- No constitutional right exercised: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 8 (1b)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because a constitutional right was exercised (Art 336(1)(b))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS FALSE
        `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS TRUE
        `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 8 (1b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice given exclusively to thwart claims from the employment: abusive, Art 336(1)(c).
`As the employee, case 9 (1c)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because it was given only to thwart claims (Art 336(1)(c))` WITH
        `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS TRUE
        `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 9 (1c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Thwarting claims was one purpose among others: 'ausschliesslich' is not met.
`As the employee, case 10 (1c)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because it was given only to thwart claims (Art 336(1)(c))` WITH
        `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS TRUE
        `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 10 (1c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- No purpose of thwarting claims: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 11 (1c)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because it was given only to thwart claims (Art 336(1)(c))` WITH
        `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS FALSE
        `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 11 (1c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice because the other party asserted claims from the employment in good faith: abusive, Art 336(1)(d).
`As the employee, case 12 (1d)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because claims were asserted in good faith (Art 336(1)(d))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS TRUE
        `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 12 (1d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Claims asserted, but not in good faith ('nach Treu und Glauben' not met): not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 13 (1d)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because claims were asserted in good faith (Art 336(1)(d))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS TRUE
        `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 13 (1d)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- No claims asserted: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 14 (1d)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because claims were asserted in good faith (Art 336(1)(d))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS FALSE
        `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 14 (1d)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military service: abusive, Art 336(1)(e).
`As the employee, case 15 (1e)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of service or a legal duty (Art 336(1)(e))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS FALSE
        `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 15 (1e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Notice because of compulsory civil protection service (Schutzdienst): abusive.
`As the employee, case 16 (1e)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of service or a legal duty (Art 336(1)(e))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS FALSE
        `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 16 (1e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Notice because of civilian service (Zivildienst): abusive. The adjective 'obligatorischen' is read as covering military and civil protection service only (fork F7); the case shows civilian service needs no 'compulsory'.
`As the employee, case 17 (1e)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of service or a legal duty (Art 336(1)(e))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS FALSE
        `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 17 (1e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Notice because of a legal duty not voluntarily assumed: abusive.
`As the employee, case 18 (1e)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of service or a legal duty (Art 336(1)(e))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS TRUE
        `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 18 (1e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A legal duty that was voluntarily assumed: 'nicht freiwillig übernommen' is not met.
`As the employee, case 19 (1e)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of service or a legal duty (Art 336(1)(e))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS TRUE
        `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 19 (1e)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- None of the service or duty grounds: not abusive on this limb (a voluntary assumption on its own is no ground).
`As the employee, case 20 (1e)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive because of service or a legal duty (Art 336(1)(e))` WITH
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS FALSE
        `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 20 (1e)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Employer's notice because the employee belongs to an employees' association: abusive, Art 336(2)(a). Mirror: the employer's seat reads the same facts.
`As the employee, case 21 (2a)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because of my union membership or activity (Art 336(2)(a))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 21 (2a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Employer's notice because the employee does not belong to an employees' association: abusive ('angehört oder nicht angehört').
`As the employee, case 22 (2a)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because of my union membership or activity (Art 336(2)(a))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 22 (2a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Employer's notice because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity: abusive.
`As the employee, case 23 (2a)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because of my union membership or activity (Art 336(2)(a))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 23 (2a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Employer's notice with none of these reasons: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 24 (2a)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because of my union membership or activity (Art 336(2)(a))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 24 (2a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice given by the employee: Art 336(2) speaks only of the employer's notice ('durch den Arbeitgeber'), so the paragraph says nothing about it, whatever the reasons.
`As the employee, case 25 (2a)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because of my union membership or activity (Art 336(2)(a))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 25 (2a)` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Employer's notice while the employee is an elected representative in a body of the business; no justified reason proved: abusive, Art 336(2)(b).
`As the employee, case 26 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 26 (2b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The representative sits in an institution connected with the undertaking: also covered.
`As the employee, case 27 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS TRUE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 27 (2b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The employer proves a justified reason: the last limb ('und der Arbeitgeber nicht beweisen kann') is not met.
`As the employee, case 28 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS TRUE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 28 (2b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The employee is not a representative: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 29 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 29 (2b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- After a transfer the mandate ended; the notice is given on the last day the mandate would have lasted: Art 336(3) keeps the protection ('so lange ... als das Mandat gedauert hätte', inclusive).
`As the employee, case 30 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS TRUE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 30 6 2027
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 30 6 2027
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 30 (2b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- After a transfer, the notice is given the day before the mandate would have ended: protected.
`As the employee, case 31 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS TRUE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 29 6 2027
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 30 6 2027
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 31 (2b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- After a transfer, the notice is given the day after the mandate would have ended: the protection has ended.
`As the employee, case 32 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS TRUE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 7 2027
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 30 6 2027
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 32 (2b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- After a transfer, within the period, but the employer proves a justified reason: not abusive.
`As the employee, case 33 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS TRUE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS TRUE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 29 6 2027
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 30 6 2027
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 33 (2b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice given by the employee: Art 336(2) does not speak of it.
`As the employee, case 34 (2b)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 34 (2b)` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Mass dismissal, the employee representation exists and was not consulted: abusive, Art 336(2)(c). Mirror: two-month cap in scenario 54.
`As the employee, case 35 (2c)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS TRUE
        `the employees have an employee representation` IS TRUE
        `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
        `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 35 (2c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Mass dismissal, the representation was consulted: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 36 (2c)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS TRUE
        `the employees have an employee representation` IS TRUE
        `the employee representation was consulted` IS TRUE
        `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 36 (2c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Mass dismissal, no representation and the employees were not consulted: abusive.
`As the employee, case 37 (2c)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS TRUE
        `the employees have an employee representation` IS FALSE
        `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
        `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 37 (2c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Mass dismissal, no representation, the employees were consulted: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 38 (2c)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS TRUE
        `the employees have an employee representation` IS FALSE
        `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
        `the employees were consulted` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 38 (2c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Mass dismissal, a representation exists and was not consulted, though the employees were: 'falls es keine solche gibt' limits the employees' consultation to the case of no representation, so abusive.
`As the employee, case 39 (2c)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS TRUE
        `the employees have an employee representation` IS TRUE
        `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
        `the employees were consulted` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 39 (2c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- No mass dismissal: not abusive on this limb.
`As the employee, case 40 (2c)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS FALSE
        `the employees have an employee representation` IS TRUE
        `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
        `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 40 (2c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice given by the employee: Art 336(2) does not speak of it.
`As the employee, case 41 (2c)` MEANS
    `Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS TRUE
        `the employees have an employee representation` IS FALSE
        `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
        `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 41 (2c)` EQUALS NOTHING

-- A ground of paragraph 1 is met (employer's notice).
`As the employee, case 42 (9)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive on a ground Art 336 lists` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS TRUE
        `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS FALSE
        `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS FALSE
        `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS FALSE
        `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS FALSE
        `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS FALSE
        `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS FALSE
        `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
        `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
        `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS FALSE
        `the employees have an employee representation` IS FALSE
        `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
        `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `As the employee, case 42 (9)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A ground of paragraph 2 is met (employer's notice).
`As the employee, case 43 (9)` MEANS
    `Is the notice abusive on a ground Art 336 lists` WITH
        `my employer gave the notice` IS TRUE
        `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS FALSE
        `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS FALSE
        `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS FALSE
        `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS FALSE
